@section('content')
  <h1>{{ $title }}</h1>
  <p>The panel tells the user what happened with a message, and with the errors on a form.</p>

  <h2>Flash messages</h2>
  <p>After a change, the panel redirects to the list and shows one message above the content:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>Record created.</code> after a create.</li>
    <li><code>Changes saved.</code> after an update.</li>
    <li><code>Record deleted.</code> after a delete.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A message shows once, on the next page the user loads. It is kept in a signed cookie, so the server holds no state for it.</p>

  <h2>Form errors</h2>
  <p>A form that does not validate shows its messages under the fields, and keeps the values the user typed. See <a href="/docs/forms">Forms</a>.</p>

  <h2>Sign-in errors</h2>
  <p>A wrong email or password shows <code>The email or password is incorrect.</code> on the sign-in page. See <a href="/docs/panel">Panel</a>.</p>

  <h2>Server errors</h2>
  <p>A row that does not exist gets a 404 page. A database error gets a 500 page, and the error is logged, not shown to the user.</p>

  <h2>Not built yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your own messages.</strong> The panel sets its three messages itself. An app cannot set a flash message in v1.</li>
    <li><strong>Toasts.</strong> Messages appear in the page and do not fade away.</li>
  </ul>
@endsection
